{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"The claim is **too underspecified to judge**: it depends on the country, year, and definition of income—individual earnings, household income, or income per person.\n\nIf you mean the **United States**, the claim is generally false: Black households have historically had a lower median household income than the national median. However, median household income does not directly establish a claim about *mean* individual income.\n\nA proper assessment would compare the same income measure, population, and year. Even a verified group average would tell you little about any particular individual’s income."}}
